{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "triage_result_schema.json",
  "$comment": "Documentation/reference schema only -- NOT wired into runtime jsonschema validation (see agents/triage/triage_result.py for the canonical, enforced Pydantic contract; this file is generated from that module's model_json_schema() output, field-for-field, not hand-invented). Generated 2026-09 during Triage Result migration Phase 5B from TriageAgentSuccessOutput and TriageAgentErrorOutput in agents/triage/triage_result.py -- the canonical shape of agents.triage.soc_triage_agent.TriageAgent.triage()'s real return value (fresh or cache-served). Does NOT model deep_triage_supplement()'s output, alert_triage.py's pre-ingest verdict, or workflow/engine.py's flattened Reporting handoff -- see that module's docstring for why each is a separate concern. Regenerated 2026-09 for Triage upgrade Step 1 ([FYP-TRIAGE-STEP1]): additive evidence_packet/assessment top-level fields and ticket.disposition/uncertainty, plus their nested Evidence*/Triage* definitions, from the same model_json_schema() output. Regenerated 2026-10 for Triage upgrade Step 2 ([FYP-TRIAGE-STEP2]): additive, required evidence_packet.raw_alerts (EvidenceRawAlerts definition, raw-alert fetch status + digest) from the same model_json_schema() output; rule_signals.lolbas is an ordinary EvidenceLeaf under the existing keyed map.",
  "description": "A validated TriageAgent.triage() return is exactly one of: TriageAgentSuccessOutput (successful run, error=null) or TriageAgentErrorOutput (exception branch, error=<message>). See `oneOf` below.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageAgentSuccessOutput"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageAgentErrorOutput"
    }
  ],
  "$defs": {
    "TriageMetakeysPayload": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Mirrors TriageAgent.triage()'s `metakeys_payload` dict exactly\n(soc_triage_agent.py:1412-1423). `extra=\"forbid\"` -- see\n`TriageRiskRating` for rationale.",
      "properties": {
        "incident_id": {
          "title": "Incident Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "incident_title": {
          "title": "Incident Title",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "timestamp": {
          "title": "Timestamp",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "matched_metakeys": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Matched Metakeys",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "metakey_values": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Metakey Values",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "ioc_summary": {
          "title": "Ioc Summary",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "risk_level": {
          "title": "Risk Level",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "classification": {
          "title": "Classification",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "mitre_tactic": {
          "title": "Mitre Tactic",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "mitre_technique": {
          "title": "Mitre Technique",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "incident_id",
        "incident_title",
        "timestamp",
        "matched_metakeys",
        "metakey_values",
        "ioc_summary",
        "risk_level",
        "classification",
        "mitre_tactic",
        "mitre_technique"
      ],
      "title": "TriageMetakeysPayload",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageRiskRating": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Mirrors TriageAgent.triage()'s `ticket[\"risk_rating\"]` dict exactly\n(soc_triage_agent.py:1434-1440). All five sub-fields are always strings\n-- each is populated via `risk_data.get(...) or \"—\"` (or, for\n`rationale`, `or \"\"`), so none of them are ever absent or non-string on\na successful triage run.\n\n`extra=\"forbid\"`: an unrecognised key here (e.g. a `confidence` score\nthe LLM prompt starts emitting) must fail loudly rather than be\nsilently dropped on re-serialization -- silent dropping would hide\nproducer/schema drift from whoever reads the validated result.",
      "properties": {
        "likelihood_initiation": {
          "title": "Likelihood Initiation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "likelihood_occurrence": {
          "title": "Likelihood Occurrence",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "likelihood_adverse_impact": {
          "title": "Likelihood Adverse Impact",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "overall_risk": {
          "title": "Overall Risk",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "rationale": {
          "title": "Rationale",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "likelihood_initiation",
        "likelihood_occurrence",
        "likelihood_adverse_impact",
        "overall_risk",
        "rationale"
      ],
      "title": "TriageRiskRating",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageTicket": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Mirrors TriageAgent.triage()'s `ticket` dict exactly\n(soc_triage_agent.py:1427-1452).\n\nNote `classification` here is `classification.upper()` (e.g. \"HIGH\"),\na different casing from `TriageMetakeysPayload.classification` (the\nlowercase `risk_level`-derived value, e.g. \"high\") -- both are real,\nindependently-set values in the live producer, not a bug this contract\nshould paper over.\n\n`extra=\"forbid\"` -- see `TriageRiskRating` for rationale.",
      "properties": {
        "unc": {
          "title": "Unc",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "incident_id": {
          "title": "Incident Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "title": {
          "title": "Title",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "incident_time": {
          "title": "Incident Time",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "created_at": {
          "title": "Created At",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "classification": {
          "title": "Classification",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "risk_rating": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageRiskRating"
        },
        "incident_category": {
          "title": "Incident Category",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "mitre_tactic": {
          "title": "Mitre Tactic",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "mitre_technique": {
          "title": "Mitre Technique",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "initial_response_time": {
          "title": "Initial Response Time",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "summary": {
          "title": "Summary",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "recommended_actions": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Recommended Actions",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "matched_ioc_count": {
          "title": "Matched Ioc Count",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "metakeys": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Metakeys",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "disposition": {
          "enum": [
            "true_positive",
            "false_positive",
            "benign_expected",
            "needs_info"
          ],
          "title": "Disposition",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "uncertainty": {
          "enum": [
            "low",
            "medium",
            "high"
          ],
          "title": "Uncertainty",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "unc",
        "incident_id",
        "title",
        "incident_time",
        "created_at",
        "classification",
        "risk_rating",
        "incident_category",
        "mitre_tactic",
        "mitre_technique",
        "initial_response_time",
        "summary",
        "recommended_actions",
        "matched_ioc_count",
        "metakeys",
        "disposition",
        "uncertainty"
      ],
      "title": "TriageTicket",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageAgentSuccessOutput": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Canonical shape of a successful (non-error) `TriageAgent.triage()`\nreturn value -- covers both a freshly-computed run (`result`,\nsoc_triage_agent.py:1456-1462) and a cache-served run (`cached`,\nsoc_triage_agent.py:1343-1348), which share the identical field set\nplus one additive marker (see `cached` below).\n\n`extra=\"forbid\"` at the top level too -- see `TriageRiskRating` for\nrationale. Note this does NOT cover `mock_triage_result()`\n(workflow/engine.py) -- that offline substitute is a *different*,\ndeliberately-mocked producer outside this contract's stated scope (see\nmodule docstring), and its own `\"mock\": True` marker key is stripped\nbefore validation at its one call site rather than modelled here.",
      "properties": {
        "metakeys_payload": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageMetakeysPayload"
        },
        "ticket": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageTicket"
        },
        "trace": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          },
          "title": "Trace",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "used_parsed_context": {
          "title": "Used Parsed Context",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "evidence_packet": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidencePacket"
        },
        "assessment": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageAssessment"
        },
        "error": {
          "default": null,
          "title": "Error",
          "type": "null"
        },
        "cached": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Cached",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "metakeys_payload",
        "ticket",
        "trace",
        "used_parsed_context",
        "evidence_packet",
        "assessment"
      ],
      "title": "TriageAgentSuccessOutput",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageAgentErrorOutput": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Canonical shape of `TriageAgent.triage()`'s exception-branch return\n(soc_triage_agent.py:1403-1407).\n\nDeliberately NOT the same shape as `TriageAgentSuccessOutput` with\nfields loosened to Optional: the real error branch returns genuinely\nempty `{}` dicts for `metakeys_payload`/`ticket` (no classification/\nticket was ever produced), and -- unlike the success path -- never sets\n`used_parsed_context` at all, so that field has no place on this model.\n`trace` may be non-empty here: an exception raised partway through\nPhase 2 or 3 still returns whatever steps Phase 1/2 already appended.\n\n`extra=\"forbid\"`: the real error branch (soc_triage_agent.py:1406-1409)\nalways constructs exactly these four keys -- no other call site feeds a\ndict with diagnostic extras into `validate_triage_agent_output()` --\nso there is no historical/error-path compatibility evidence requiring\na looser policy here. Should a genuine need for extra diagnostic\nfields on the error path emerge later, loosen this deliberately then,\nwith that evidence recorded here.",
      "properties": {
        "error": {
          "title": "Error",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "metakeys_payload": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Metakeys Payload",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "ticket": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Ticket",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "trace": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          },
          "title": "Trace",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "error"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceBaseline": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The measured historical prior (agents/triage/baseline.py).",
      "properties": {
        "status": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "reason": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_source_entity_7d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_source_entity_30d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_source_entity_90d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_source_entity_all_time": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_source_entity_annualized": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_entity_7d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_entity_30d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_entity_90d": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "same_entity_all_time": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "first_seen": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "last_seen": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "is_first_occurrence": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "is_known_noisy": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "coverage_start": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "coverage_end": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "status",
        "reason",
        "same_source_entity_7d",
        "same_source_entity_30d",
        "same_source_entity_90d",
        "same_source_entity_all_time",
        "same_source_entity_annualized",
        "same_entity_7d",
        "same_entity_30d",
        "same_entity_90d",
        "same_entity_all_time",
        "first_seen",
        "last_seen",
        "is_first_occurrence",
        "is_known_noisy",
        "coverage_start",
        "coverage_end"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceBaseline",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceContext": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Business context. Always status \"missing\" in Step 1 (placeholders\nfilled by later steps) -- so benign_expected is unreachable by design.",
      "properties": {
        "asset_context": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "change_context": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "confirmed_benign_history": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "asset_context",
        "change_context",
        "confirmed_benign_history"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceContext",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceDataQuality": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Parsing-stage data quality, copied from parsed_context.",
      "properties": {
        "parser_status": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "parser_confidence": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "missing_fields": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "data_quality": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "parser_status",
        "parser_confidence",
        "missing_fields",
        "data_quality"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceDataQuality",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceDetection": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "What fired: NetWitness incident-level detection facts.",
      "properties": {
        "createdBy": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "ruleId": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "created": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "sources": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "riskScore": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "priority": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "alertCount": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "eventCount": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "tactics": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "techniques": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "createdBy",
        "ruleId",
        "created",
        "sources",
        "riskScore",
        "priority",
        "alertCount",
        "eventCount",
        "tactics",
        "techniques"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceDetection",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceEntity": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The resolved primary entity and its kind (ip_internal/ip_external/\nhostname/user/file/unresolved).",
      "properties": {
        "value": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        },
        "kind": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value",
        "kind"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceEntity",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidenceLeaf": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One citable fact in the evidence packet. `status` says how it is\nknown: measured (observed), inferred (derived by code) or missing\n(unknown -- never to be read as \"safe\").",
      "properties": {
        "value": {
          "default": null,
          "title": "Value"
        },
        "status": {
          "enum": [
            "measured",
            "inferred",
            "missing"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "status",
        "source"
      ],
      "title": "EvidenceLeaf",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvidencePacket": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "[FYP-EVALUATOR] The whole evidence packet. `rule_signals` is keyed by\nindicator label (plus `scan_summary`, and from Step 2 `lolbas`) because\nthe set of deterministic hits varies per incident; every other section\nhas a fixed field set.",
      "properties": {
        "detection": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceDetection"
        },
        "entity": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceEntity"
        },
        "data_quality": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceDataQuality"
        },
        "baseline": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceBaseline"
        },
        "raw_alerts": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceRawAlerts"
        },
        "rule_signals": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceLeaf"
          },
          "title": "Rule Signals",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "context": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceContext"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "detection",
        "entity",
        "data_quality",
        "baseline",
        "raw_alerts",
        "context"
      ],
      "title": "EvidencePacket",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageAssessment": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "[FYP-EVALUATOR] Disposition + the reasoning trail behind it.\n\n`proposed_disposition` is what the model proposed; `disposition` is what\nsurvived citation verification and the guards in agents/triage/guards.py\n(every change is listed in `guard_actions`).",
      "properties": {
        "disposition": {
          "enum": [
            "true_positive",
            "false_positive",
            "benign_expected",
            "needs_info"
          ],
          "title": "Disposition",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "proposed_disposition": {
          "enum": [
            "true_positive",
            "false_positive",
            "benign_expected",
            "needs_info"
          ],
          "title": "Proposed Disposition",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "uncertainty": {
          "enum": [
            "low",
            "medium",
            "high"
          ],
          "title": "Uncertainty",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "hypotheses": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageHypotheses"
        },
        "lookalike_ruled_out": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageLookalike"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "fn_cost_if_wrong": {
          "title": "Fn Cost If Wrong",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "evidence_checked": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Evidence Checked",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "citation_errors": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageCitationError"
          },
          "title": "Citation Errors",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "guard_actions": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TriageGuardAction"
          },
          "title": "Guard Actions",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "disposition",
        "proposed_disposition",
        "uncertainty",
        "hypotheses",
        "fn_cost_if_wrong",
        "evidence_checked",
        "citation_errors",
        "guard_actions"
      ],
      "title": "TriageAssessment",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriageCitationError": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A citation removed by verify_citations(): `error` is\n\"unknown_path\" or \"missing_status\" (or \"uncited_claim_dropped\").",
      "properties": {
